# Arden OS Security

Security is part of system architecture.

Threat assumptions:

- userspace may be malicious
- applications may be buggy
- network traffic is hostile
- files may be corrupted
- packages may be malicious
- devices may fail
- DMA may be dangerous
- concurrent code may race

Security objectives:

- kernel/user separation
- process isolation
- capabilities
- permissions
- secure handles
- memory protection
- ASLR
- NX
- sandboxing
- package verification
- update verification
- secure boot
- encrypted storage
- audit logging

Every privileged subsystem requires security review.
